-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/21b4dea9-23b7-5850-95e1-b2c4e7292a9c
-- title:
--   Coaction of the subgroup Hopf algebra on the levels B[[x]]/I^N
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $B$ a commutative ring, and $X$ a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $B$ in the sense of the structure `FormalODModule` (a two-dimensional commutative formal group law $F = X.F$ together with a $\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$-action and a uniformiser series, all by law homomorphisms); only the group law $F$ enters the statement. Let $I \subseteq B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]$ be an ideal such that some power $x_i^q$ lies in $I$ for $i = 1,2$, and such that for every $f \in I$ the series $f(F(x,y))$ lies in the ideal of $B[\![x,y]\!]$ (four variables, indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,2 \oplus \mathrm{Fin}\,2$) generated by the images of $I$ under the two coordinate inclusions $x_i \mapsto x_i$ and $x_i \mapsto y_i$. Let $L$ be a commutative Hopf algebra over $B$ and $\pi : B[\![x_1,x_2]\!] \to L$ a surjective $B$-algebra map with kernel $I$ such that each $\pi(x_i)$ is nilpotent, such that $\pi$ is adic evaluation at the point $(\pi(x_1),\pi(x_2))$ for the zero ideal of $L$ (so $\pi G = G(\pi x)$ for every $G$), such that the comultiplication satisfies $\Delta(\pi(x_i)) = F_i(\pi x \otimes 1,\, 1 \otimes \pi x)$ computed by adic evaluation in $L \otimes_B L$ at the zero ideal, and such that the counit satisfies $\varepsilon(\pi G) = G(0)$ (the constant coefficient). Let $N \neq 0$ and put $S := B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]/I^N$. Then there is a $B$-algebra homomorphism $\delta : S \to S \otimes_B L$ with the following five properties: (i) for every $G$, $\delta(\bar G)$ is the adic evaluation of $G$ at the zero ideal of $S \otimes_B L$ at the point whose $i$-th coordinate is the adic evaluation of $F_i$ at $(\bar x_j \otimes 1,\, 1 \otimes \pi x_j)$, i.e. $\delta(\bar G) = G\bigl(F(\bar x \otimes 1, 1 \otimes \pi x)\bigr)$; (ii) coassociativity, namely $(\delta \otimes \mathrm{id}_L)\circ\delta$ followed by the associator $(S \otimes L)\otimes L \cong S \otimes (L \otimes L)$ agrees with $(\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \Delta)\circ\delta$; (iii) counitality, $(\mathrm{id}_S \otimes \varepsilon)(\delta s) = s \otimes 1$ in $S \otimes_B B$; (iv) for every $k$ and every $f \in I^k$, $\delta(\bar f)$ lies in the ideal of $S \otimes_B L$ generated by $\{s \otimes 1 : s \in \text{image of } I^k \text{ in } S\}$; and (v) for every $G$, applying $\tilde\pi \otimes \mathrm{id}_L$ to $\delta(\bar G)$, where $\tilde\pi : S \to L$ is the map induced by $\pi$ (legitimate since $I^N \subseteq I = \ker \pi$), returns $\Delta(\pi G)$.
--
--   This exhibits each level $B[\![x_1,x_2]\!]/I^N$ of a subgroup ideal $I$ of the formal group law of $X$ as a comodule algebra over the Hopf algebra $L$ of the corresponding finite infinitesimal subgroup, the coaction being evaluation at the nilpotent point $F(\bar x \otimes 1, 1 \otimes \pi x)$, compatibly with the $I$-adic filtration and with the comultiplication of $L$. It is used in the analysis of invariants for such subgroups, by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.eq_span_setOf_invariant_of_subgroup_ideal_of_free), [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_mem_pow_and_invariant_succ`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_mem_pow_and_invariant_succ) and [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_sub_mem_and_firstOrder_invariant`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_sub_mem_and_firstOrder_invariant).
